  "Question": "Which method should be used to solve \\(3x²=6x\\)? Which of the following is most suitable?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Factoring",
    "B": "Taking square roots directly",
    "C": "Completing the square",
    "D": "Using the quadratic formula"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Moving terms gives \\(3x²-6x=0\\). Factoring out the common factor gives \\(3x(x-2)=0\\), so \\(x=0\\) or \\(2\\). Factoring is the simplest method.",
